==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈspɪ.t(ə)l/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spittle.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪtəl|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
Alteration of dialectal {{m|en|spattle}} (by association with {{m|en|spit#Etymology_2|pos=noun}}), from {{inh|en|ang|spātl}}, which is related to {{m|ang|spǣtan}} (whence {{m|en|spit#Etymology_2|pos=verb}}).

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[spit|Spit]], usually [[frothy]] and of a [[milky]] [[coloration]].
# Something frothy and [[white]] that resembles spit.
# [[spit-up|Spit-up]] or [[drool]] of an [[infant]].

